  "notes": [
    "**Venir** is highly irregular in multiple tenses",
    "Present: stem change e→ie (except nosotros) plus irregular \"yo\" form (vengo)",
    "Preterite: completely irregular stem \"vin-\"",
    "Imperfect: regular -IR pattern with accent on \"í\"",
    "Pretérito Perfecto: regular past participle **venido**",
    "Future: irregular stem \"vendr-\" (not \"venir-\")",
    "Condicional: irregular stem \"vendr-\" + conditional endings",
    "Opposite of **ir** (to go)",
    "Common usage: *venir a casa* (to come home), *venir de España* (to come from Spain)",
    "Often used with gerund: *Vengo corriendo* (I'm coming running / I come running)"
  ],
